1
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,120
Chinese.

2
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:01,799
Chinese.

3
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:03,599
What are you looking at?

4
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,439
Pick it up.

5
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:05,879
Pick it up!

6
00:02:07,159 --> 00:02:07,879
Clean it up.

7
00:02:49,319 --> 00:02:51,319
Chinese? Eat up.

8
00:03:40,759 --> 00:03:41,159
It looks nice.

9
00:03:42,759 --> 00:03:43,159
Not bad.

10
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:50,080
What are you looking at?

11
00:03:50,759 --> 00:03:51,960
You can find all this online back home.

12
00:03:52,639 --> 00:03:54,680
Besides, we're here on a mission.

13
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:56,879
It's precisely because we're on a mission

14
00:03:57,039 --> 00:03:58,719
that I have to get you a gift.

15
00:04:00,879 --> 00:04:01,360
This one.

16
00:04:12,039 --> 00:04:12,719
How much?

17
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,319
800 dollars.

18
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,240
What are you doing? There are so many people around!

19
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,120
Today...

20
00:04:40,959 --> 00:04:42,639
I want to officially propose to you here.

21
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:44,680
You're my girlfriend.

22
00:04:45,399 --> 00:04:46,879
We took this trip together...

23
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,720
just so I could propose to you.

24
00:04:52,759 --> 00:04:53,240
Get up!

25
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:53,920
Come on, get up!

26
00:04:55,839 --> 00:04:56,600
Just get up first!

27
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,720
Xiaobai, let me truly love you...

28
00:04:59,639 --> 00:05:00,519
and cherish you, okay?

29
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,160
You

30
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:53,120
Split up and chase them!

31
00:06:06,879 --> 00:06:07,759
Who are you?

32
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,000
Why are you following us?

33
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,240
Following you? What do you mean?

34
00:06:13,079 --> 00:06:14,240
I already gave you back your wallet!

35
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,519
What more do you want?

36
00:06:16,839 --> 00:06:17,879
You've tailed us for blocks.

37
00:06:18,199 --> 00:06:19,639
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

38
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:22,720
Fine.

39
00:06:23,439 --> 00:06:24,240
I...

40
00:06:26,079 --> 00:06:28,920
I was just trying to steal something.

41
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,120
I'm sorry.

42
00:06:36,199 --> 00:06:37,160
Please let go.

43
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,879
Fine, consider yourself lucky.

44
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:42,439
Get lost.

45
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:44,279
Don't let me catch you again.

46
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,240
Okay.

47
00:06:47,879 --> 00:06:48,639
I'm leaving then.

48
00:06:48,759 --> 00:06:49,319
Go.

49
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,120
Thanks.

50
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:52,800
Thanks.

51
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,319
Thanks, Michael.

52
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,360
Wait.

53
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,279
What did you call me?

54
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,079
Aren't you Michael?

55
00:07:06,439 --> 00:07:07,160
You speak Chinese?

56
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,360
Who told you my name is Michael?

57
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,680
Bro...

58
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:12,800
Just a little.

59
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,000
Boss!

60
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:17,399
Boss!

61
00:07:18,519 --> 00:07:19,720
Boss!

62
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,120
I told you you'd lose.

63
00:07:24,279 --> 00:07:24,560
Come on.

64
00:07:27,319 --> 00:07:27,680
Where's the money?

65
00:07:29,199 --> 00:07:30,639
Money, money, money.

66
00:07:31,079 --> 00:07:31,639
I'm done playing.

67
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,240
That's all you care about.

68
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:36,480
Just deduct it from my pay.

69
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,279
All right?

70
00:07:41,279 --> 00:07:41,879
Him?

71
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:43,240
My new partner?

72
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,120
Yeah.

73
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:45,560
His name is Tony.

74
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:46,920
He's my informant.

75
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,319
Tony, let me introduce you.

76
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:49,879
This is Zhuang Cen.

77
00:07:50,519 --> 00:07:51,920
This is Ge Xiaobai.

78
00:07:52,759 --> 00:07:53,439
Zhuang Cen.

79
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,600
Tony knows Xilano well.

80
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,000
He can help you find Ma Jingrong.

81
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:12,040
I'm talking about money. Big money.

82
00:08:13,439 --> 00:08:15,800
Serious money. Big money.

83
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:22,439
Don't worry. The guy I recommend is solid.

84
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,000
You can count on the person I found.

85
00:08:30,759 --> 00:08:33,679
Tony was an undercover cop in Xilano.

86
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,799
During a mission,

87
00:08:35,799 --> 00:08:36,919
he was forced into drug addiction.

88
00:08:40,039 --> 00:08:41,000
After the mission ended,

89
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:42,960
his cravings kicked in,

90
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,559
so he bought a large stash from dealers.

91
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:47,879
And as a result,

92
00:08:48,279 --> 00:08:49,240
he was sentenced to five years.

93
00:08:52,399 --> 00:08:53,440
After his release,

94
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,559
the Xilano Police Department

95
00:08:54,919 --> 00:08:56,320
dismissed him from the force.

96
00:08:56,919 --> 00:08:59,600
But he's a protected Country M informant.

97
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,000
Three years ago,

98
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:03,480
he came to assist us at Interpol.

99
00:09:06,159 --> 00:09:07,559
How is he doing now?

100
00:09:16,759 --> 00:09:17,960
He still hasn't kicked the habit,

101
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,879
but Tony is a solid guy.

102
00:09:20,279 --> 00:09:20,720
Also,

103
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,759
during your mission,

104
00:09:22,759 --> 00:09:24,320
never let him get near any drugs.

105
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,399
His identity as a cop...

106
00:09:33,799 --> 00:09:34,799
How many people know about it?

107
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,679
From his very first day on the force,

108
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:41,960
he worked undercover.

109
00:09:42,159 --> 00:09:44,399
He never wore a police uniform for a single day.

110
00:09:45,399 --> 00:09:46,919
His identity is classified.

111
00:09:49,799 --> 00:09:50,120
By the way,

112
00:09:50,879 --> 00:09:52,039
I just received word that

113
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,240
a repeat offender named Viskay

114
00:09:54,679 --> 00:09:56,480
is planning to rob a gang's warehouse.

115
00:09:56,799 --> 00:09:59,720
When the time comes, Tony will get you in.

116
00:10:06,159 --> 00:10:07,639
Have Zhuang Cen rob drug dealers?

117
00:10:11,159 --> 00:10:11,720
Yes.

118
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,279
As for this operation,

119
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:14,120
you don't need to worry.

120
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,159
I've coordinated with Country M police.

121
00:10:16,399 --> 00:10:18,360
Once they make their entry,

122
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,559
the Country M police will move in

123
00:10:19,639 --> 00:10:20,759
and arrest them immediately.

124
00:10:20,759 --> 00:10:22,799
Once they're sent to Xilano Prison,

125
00:10:22,799 --> 00:10:25,000
everyone will know about their crimes.

126
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:25,639
That way,

127
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:27,559
no one will ever suspect your cover.

128
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,480
The warehouse is heavily guarded at night.

129
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,879
It's actually more relaxed during the day.

130
00:10:48,879 --> 00:10:50,639
We'll pretend we're picking up goods.

131
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,000
Once inside,

132
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,480
I'll take everyone hostage.

133
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,480
You two grab the cargo.

134
00:10:55,919 --> 00:10:56,679
Open up.

135
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:04,039
Hello.

136
00:11:05,559 --> 00:11:06,480
Hello, guys.

137
00:11:08,879 --> 00:11:09,840
Relax, relax.

138
00:11:10,919 --> 00:11:12,519
A new friend to work with.

139
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,279
Let him in.

140
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,159
This is Michael. A newcomer.

141
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:28,440
Clean record.

142
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:32,960
Took a lot of effort to find him for you.

143
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:35,120
A rookie? Never done a job?

144
00:11:36,399 --> 00:11:37,559
Of course.

145
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,480
A clean record...

146
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:43,360
...means he's never been caught.

147
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,000
He's solid.

148
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,759
Do you speak Country M's language?

149
00:11:49,679 --> 00:11:52,200
A little. My English is better.

150
00:11:53,559 --> 00:11:54,519
Know how to use a gun?

151
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,000
Weren't you looking for a driver?

152
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,360
We're down a man now.

153
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,440
You'll drive when the time comes.

154
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:15,799
I only agreed to introduce someone.

155
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:17,600
I've done time.

156
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:21,480
I wouldn't dare pull this off.

157
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:27,159
What was prison like?

158
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:36,000
Can you handle a gun?

159
00:12:36,759 --> 00:12:37,240
Yes.

160
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,360
Strip it and reassemble it.

161
00:12:48,159 --> 00:12:48,720
Wait.

162
00:12:49,919 --> 00:12:50,639
Let's do it together.

163
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:58,559
One, two, three.

164
00:12:58,720 --> 00:12:59,360
Go.

165
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:12,440
I won.

166
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:19,360
This is who we need.

167
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:34,480
Zhongtian Company is a state-private mix.

168
00:13:34,919 --> 00:13:37,039
Senior cadres are on the state payroll.

169
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,519
According to the files,

170
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,559
most of them are clean.

171
00:13:41,159 --> 00:13:43,519
I think we can start by looking into

172
00:13:43,519 --> 00:13:44,879
Zhou Fuhai's assets.

173
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,000
If we investigate,

174
00:13:46,159 --> 00:13:47,159
we can make a bigger move.

175
00:13:47,639 --> 00:13:48,879
Let's see which parts of Zhongtian Company

176
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:51,480
are deliberately covering up

177
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,399
Chen Hai's drug trafficking network.

178
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:53,840
Understood.

179
00:13:55,159 --> 00:13:55,840
Also,

180
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:58,279
Li Qiang used to work under Chen Hai.

181
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,720
I was wondering if

182
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,039
he might go to Chen Hai right now.

183
00:14:02,519 --> 00:14:03,480
Should we tail him?

184
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:06,039
Li Qiang is desperate to sell and run.

185
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,159
Unless forced into a corner,

186
00:14:07,399 --> 00:14:09,080
he won't contact Chen Hai at all.

187
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:11,320
All the clues pointing to Chen Hai

188
00:14:11,519 --> 00:14:12,879
have only just surfaced.

189
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,279
Let's not rush it.

190
00:14:14,559 --> 00:14:15,240
Then we'll stand by.

191
00:14:15,759 --> 00:14:16,120
Right.

192
00:14:16,639 --> 00:14:17,120
Understood.

193
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,600
Report any new developments to me immediately.

194
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:22,240
Yes, sir.

195
00:14:23,519 --> 00:14:24,080
Lao Huang.

196
00:14:24,639 --> 00:14:25,919
Look at how long you've been on the phone.

197
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:28,120
Your noodles are clumped up, and you still haven't eaten.

198
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:29,799
I'm working, aren't I?

199
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:32,399
Work, work, work.

200
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:34,279
That's all you think about all day.

201
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:35,879
Even if you don't rest,

202
00:14:36,039 --> 00:14:37,519
your subordinates are getting worn out too.

203
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,720
They're passionate about their work.

204
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:40,799
I can't just stop them.

205
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:41,679
Besides,

206
00:14:41,679 --> 00:14:42,919
with so many cases right now,

207
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,559
how can we get the job done if I don't push?

208
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,159
All you care about is the job.

209
00:14:46,759 --> 00:14:48,600
You've never given me peace of mind.

210
00:14:48,799 --> 00:14:49,840
Day in and day out,

211
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:52,000
how often do I even get to see you?

212
00:14:52,799 --> 00:14:54,080
All right, all right.

213
00:14:55,039 --> 00:14:56,519
If it weren't for you

214
00:14:56,519 --> 00:14:58,480
dedicating yourself fully to our family,

215
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:01,879
how could I focus on my work, right?

216
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,200
You're the real hero here.

217
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,840
Stop sweet-talking me.

218
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:07,720
Come on.

219
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,519
Go eat your noodles.

220
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,200
By the way,

221
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:14,720
a few days ago,

222
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,320
I ran into Tian Zheng's daughter.

223
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:18,919
Tian Xin.

224
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:23,200
I haven't seen her in years.

225
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:23,840
Oh, and another thing.

226
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,320
The two of them are dating.

227
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:27,759
Which two?

228
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:30,200
Tian Xin and our Xiaoxiao.

229
00:15:30,559 --> 00:15:31,360
Really?

230
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,360
They actually make a good match.

231
00:15:37,399 --> 00:15:39,639
You haven't seen Tian Xin in over a decade.

232
00:15:39,639 --> 00:15:41,039
How do you know they're a good match?

233
00:15:41,799 --> 00:15:42,440
Let me tell you,

234
00:15:42,799 --> 00:15:44,840
they seem to have had a little fight lately.

235
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,840
What fight?

236
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:51,200
Our Xiaoxiao is being too picky.

237
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,559
What are you talking about?

238
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,399
He's lucky Tian Xin isn't picky about him.

239
00:15:56,399 --> 00:15:57,519
It's the girl

240
00:15:57,679 --> 00:15:59,399
who thinks Xiaoxiao's job is too dangerous.

241
00:15:59,639 --> 00:16:02,320
Her father died in the line of duty.

242
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,840
Why not just have Li Xiao change jobs?

243
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,799
With your seniority after all these years,

244
00:16:10,799 --> 00:16:11,480
if you pulled a few strings,

245
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:13,240
you could easily find him a good job.

246
00:16:16,279 --> 00:16:17,919
You've been with me for so many years,

247
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,919
why hasn't your mindset improved at all?

248
00:16:20,159 --> 00:16:21,240
If we follow your logic,

249
00:16:21,399 --> 00:16:22,559
whenever someone at the bureau dates

250
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:23,840
and their partner demands this,

251
00:16:24,039 --> 00:16:25,360
who would still be a cop?

252
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:28,480
Either way, I just don't like

253
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,480
our Xiaoxiao working as a cop.

254
00:16:29,879 --> 00:16:30,600
Let me tell you,

255
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,399
you have to look out for him at work.

256
00:16:33,039 --> 00:16:34,159
If anything happens to him

257
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,320
under your watch,

258
00:16:35,639 --> 00:16:37,320
you couldn't face his parents.

259
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,440
What kind of talk is that?

260
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:41,000
So many eyes are watching me at the bureau.

261
00:16:41,159 --> 00:16:42,879
Can I openly favor my own nephew?

262
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:46,039
I'm only looking out for your family.

263
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,080
Take it or leave it.

264
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,919
Alright, alright, stop eating.

265
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,679
What are you doing? I haven't eaten yet.

266
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:55,200
A little bickering and you take my food?

267
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:55,879
Look at this.

268
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:57,480
It's congealed. How can you eat that?

269
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,440
No worries, no worries.

270
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,720
I'll fix you a fresh bowl.

271
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:02,759
By the way,

272
00:17:03,039 --> 00:17:04,160
isn't tomorrow Sunday?

273
00:17:04,759 --> 00:17:06,720
Tell Li Xiao to bring Tian Xin for dinner.

274
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,400
Haven't seen her in years,

275
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,240
and I really miss that girl.

276
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,559
Alright, got it.

277
00:17:36,359 --> 00:17:36,799
Who's this?

278
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,079
Boss, it's Guan Qiang.

279
00:17:39,519 --> 00:17:39,880
Captain Bai.

280
00:17:40,279 --> 00:17:41,119
Regarding the logistics company case,

281
00:17:41,119 --> 00:17:42,160
something new has come up.

282
00:17:42,319 --> 00:17:42,920
Captain Lu wants to know

283
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,519
if you can return for an urgent meeting.

284
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,240
I'll be there in 15 minutes.

285
00:17:46,559 --> 00:17:46,880
Got it.

286
00:18:17,319 --> 00:18:17,960
He Yong.

287
00:18:19,359 --> 00:18:20,440
What are you doing here?

288
00:18:23,279 --> 00:18:24,839
How many times do I have to tell you?

289
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:27,480
I'm really working overtime for my job.

290
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:28,799
What's this supposed to mean?

291
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:29,599
Checking up on me?

292
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:42,799
Happy birthday, Mom!

293
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:51,319
Happy birthday to you

294
00:18:51,599 --> 00:18:55,680
Happy birthday to you

295
00:18:55,799 --> 00:19:00,160
Happy birthday to you

296
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,599
Happy birthday, Captain Bai!

297
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,039
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

298
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:08,400
Today is your birthday,

299
00:19:08,720 --> 00:19:09,440
and our daughter wanted to see you,

300
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,279
so I didn't tell you in advance.

301
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:12,720
Happy birthday.

302
00:19:17,599 --> 00:19:18,799
What are you guys doing?

303
00:19:19,599 --> 00:19:20,599
This is the police department.

304
00:19:21,079 --> 00:19:22,480
You're breaking protocol, you know?

305
00:19:23,279 --> 00:19:24,000
Captain Bai,

306
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,480
if Director Huang comes down on us,

307
00:19:27,119 --> 00:19:29,599
Captain Lu said he'd take the blame.

308
00:19:31,839 --> 00:19:33,279
I already cleared it with Director Huang.

309
00:19:33,319 --> 00:19:33,759
We're fine.

310
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,039
Thank you, everyone.

311
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,359
Mom, make a wish!

312
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,799
Make a wish with Mommy, okay?

313
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:45,559
Okay.

314
00:19:52,079 --> 00:19:55,119
Happy birthday to you

315
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:58,519
Happy birthday to you

316
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:02,519
Happy birthday to you

317
00:20:03,039 --> 00:20:07,359
Happy birthday to you

318
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:11,960
Let's blow out the candles with Daddy, okay?

319
00:20:12,079 --> 00:20:12,720
Okay.

320
00:20:14,279 --> 00:20:16,920
One, two, three!

321
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:23,880
Happy birthday!

322
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:27,039
She's asleep.

323
00:20:33,519 --> 00:20:34,319
If something's on your mind, say it.

324
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:40,319
Go ahead.

325
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:45,319
Thank you.

326
00:20:46,559 --> 00:20:47,759
Geez, you scared me to death!

327
00:20:49,359 --> 00:20:50,079
To be honest,

328
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:53,039
conspiring with your team

329
00:20:53,039 --> 00:20:54,000
to throw you a birthday party...

330
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,480
My heart was pounding the whole time,

331
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:56,519
terrified you'd get angry.

332
00:20:59,839 --> 00:21:01,440
Is my image in your mind

333
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:02,599
really that rigid?

334
00:21:02,839 --> 00:21:03,480
Not rigid at all.

335
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:06,000
Formidable, and a bit stern.

336
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,440
Having such a formidable wife,

337
00:21:11,279 --> 00:21:12,160
you must feel pretty wronged, right?

338
00:21:12,599 --> 00:21:14,039
Incredibly wronged.

339
00:21:15,279 --> 00:21:15,799
Though,

340
00:21:16,319 --> 00:21:17,799
wronged, but happy.

341
00:21:18,559 --> 00:21:19,640
Let me tell you something.

342
00:21:21,519 --> 00:21:23,640
Huanhuan wrote an essay the other day.

343
00:21:23,839 --> 00:21:27,079
The teacher had them pick one parent to write about.

344
00:21:27,359 --> 00:21:28,640
I thought she'd definitely write about me.

345
00:21:29,119 --> 00:21:31,079
Turns out your daughter titled her essay,

346
00:21:31,319 --> 00:21:32,519
"My Police Officer Mom."

347
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:35,039
Looks like this dad of hers

348
00:21:35,319 --> 00:21:36,640
in our daughter's eyes

349
00:21:37,559 --> 00:21:39,720
isn't nearly as heroic as Captain Bai.

350
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:44,640
I'm usually busy with work

351
00:21:45,279 --> 00:21:46,319
and have no time for her,

352
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,559
but I'm truly grateful to you.

353
00:21:50,119 --> 00:21:51,680
Throughout her growing up,

354
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:53,119
you've always been by her side.

355
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:59,319
How come you haven't complained lately

356
00:21:59,319 --> 00:22:00,400
about my working overtime?

357
00:22:03,079 --> 00:22:04,000
Here's the thing.

358
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:08,799
I've been thinking about this a lot lately.

359
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:14,160
The most foolish thing for me to do

360
00:22:14,359 --> 00:22:17,200
is fight against things I can't change.

361
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
You're busy at work—I can't change that, right?

362
00:22:21,559 --> 00:22:23,000
And our bond after all these years—

363
00:22:23,039 --> 00:22:23,720
could we ever separate?

364
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:24,319
No way.

365
00:22:25,519 --> 00:22:26,640
I can't change that either.

366
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,039
So I thought,

367
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:31,880
instead of fighting with you and myself,

368
00:22:32,279 --> 00:22:33,599
I might as well go with the flow.

369
00:22:33,839 --> 00:22:34,440
Don't you think?

370
00:22:36,079 --> 00:22:37,839
Are you sure you're not just compromising?

371
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:41,400
That hurts.

372
00:22:45,119 --> 00:22:45,839
Thank you, Commander.

373
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:47,960
We're family. No need to be polite.

374
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:49,119
No formalities between family.

375
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:50,400
No formalities between family.

376
00:22:50,799 --> 00:22:51,759
Sleep, sleep, sleep.

377
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:52,880
Time for bed.

378
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,039
Um...

379
00:23:06,039 --> 00:23:07,880
My car had some trouble this morning,

380
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:10,039
so I called a ride. Is that okay?

381
00:23:10,039 --> 00:23:10,559
That's fine.

382
00:23:11,759 --> 00:23:12,559
Were you getting impatient?

383
00:23:14,359 --> 00:23:16,319
I'd never get impatient waiting for you.

384
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:18,440
Always such a sweet talker.

385
00:23:23,119 --> 00:23:23,640
Excuse me, folks.

386
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:24,599
Hurry it up.

387
00:23:24,599 --> 00:23:25,599
I have to pick up another passenger.

388
00:23:27,640 --> 00:23:28,279
Another passenger?

389
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:29,480
Didn't I book this car?

390
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:30,279
Why pick up anyone else?

391
00:23:30,559 --> 00:23:31,119
Look, buddy.

392
00:23:31,319 --> 00:23:32,880
You booked a carpool, not a private ride.

393
00:23:33,119 --> 00:23:34,039
I booked a carpool?

394
00:23:34,039 --> 00:23:34,440
Yeah.

395
00:23:41,839 --> 00:23:42,720
I must've tapped the wrong thing.

396
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,079
Can I change it?

397
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,119
Can't change it now.

398
00:23:45,119 --> 00:23:45,920
While I was waiting just now,

399
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:47,000
someone else already joined.

400
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:49,519
Where are we heading first?

401
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:51,880
We pick up someone at Wushankou first,

402
00:23:52,119 --> 00:23:53,440
then drop off whoever's closer.

403
00:23:54,799 --> 00:23:55,720
Won't this make you late?

404
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:56,680
I'm fine.

405
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:57,960
I booked an appointment online,

406
00:23:58,079 --> 00:23:58,839
so I won't have to wait in line.

407
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:00,200
How about I call another car

408
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:00,759
and let him leave?

409
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:02,160
It's fine. Come on, let's go.

410
00:24:36,359 --> 00:24:37,279
Did you call for a ride?

411
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:37,839
Yeah.

412
00:24:38,039 --> 00:24:40,039
Could you deliver something for me?

413
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:45,240
Is this address correct?

414
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:46,640
The phone number is written on it.

415
00:24:46,799 --> 00:24:47,759
Call them when you get there,

416
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:49,000
and someone will come pick it up.

417
00:24:50,519 --> 00:24:51,359
All right, sure.

418
00:25:11,359 --> 00:25:13,519
How come you're doing delivery gigs too?

419
00:25:15,119 --> 00:25:16,200
Just doing people a favor.

420
00:25:16,279 --> 00:25:17,400
Plus, it's another fare for me.

421
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:19,119
Besides, when sending stuff these days,

422
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,839
people don't even call local couriers.

423
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:23,160
They just hail a ride to deliver it.

424
00:25:23,839 --> 00:25:24,799
Whatever they ask you to deliver,

425
00:25:24,799 --> 00:25:25,960
you don't even ask what it is?

426
00:25:26,359 --> 00:25:27,599
Why would I ask?

427
00:25:27,599 --> 00:25:28,640
That's their privacy.

428
00:25:35,519 --> 00:25:35,960
Police.

429
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:37,880
I need to check this.

430
00:25:42,319 --> 00:25:43,680
I never opened that thing!

431
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:44,960
I have no idea what's inside.

432
00:25:49,279 --> 00:25:50,680
It's not state secrets in there, is it?

433
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:54,880
But that kid didn't look like a spy.

434
00:26:42,559 --> 00:26:43,119
I'm sorry.

435
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:44,599
Something has come up,

436
00:26:44,880 --> 00:26:45,720
so I can't stay with you.

437
00:26:47,799 --> 00:26:48,279
It's fine.

438
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:50,160
It's just a routine checkup anyway.

439
00:26:50,359 --> 00:26:51,519
I can head back on my own afterward.

440
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,640
I thought since it's the weekend,

441
00:26:54,759 --> 00:26:55,880
we could spend some more time together.

442
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:56,839
Turns out...

443
00:26:58,519 --> 00:26:59,640
It's fine.

444
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:01,440
Am I really that petty?

445
00:27:11,039 --> 00:27:12,200
All right, go ahead.

446
00:27:12,640 --> 00:27:13,440
Off you go.

447
00:27:16,799 --> 00:27:17,640
I'll head inside then.

448
00:27:17,920 --> 00:27:18,279
Go ahead.

449
00:27:22,319 --> 00:27:23,200
Don't forget about lunch.

450
00:27:23,839 --> 00:27:24,960
We're eating at my uncle's place.

451
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:26,519
I'll pick you up when I'm done.

452
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:27,559
No need.

453
00:27:27,559 --> 00:27:28,759
I can go myself after the checkup.

454
00:27:29,039 --> 00:27:29,759
You don't need to pick me up.

455
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:31,599
Go on.

456
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,240
I'd rather watch you leave

457
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:39,039
before I head inside.

458
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:42,279
I'm off.

459
00:28:33,559 --> 00:28:34,640
Hey, man...

460
00:28:34,799 --> 00:28:36,039
I mean, Officer...

461
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:39,039
I really have nothing to do with this.

462
00:28:39,319 --> 00:28:40,839
I was just delivering something on my way.

463
00:28:42,359 --> 00:28:44,920
Be careful carrying things for others.

464
00:28:45,839 --> 00:28:47,200
Good thing you reminded me.

465
00:28:47,839 --> 00:28:49,240
If there was a bomb in there,

466
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:50,599
I'd be a dead man!

467
00:28:52,799 --> 00:28:53,599
Once you get there,

468
00:28:53,599 --> 00:28:55,119
just hand the stuff directly to him.

469
00:28:55,119 --> 00:28:56,359
Don't worry about anything else.

470
00:28:56,640 --> 00:28:57,000
And one more thing.

471
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:57,640
In a bit,

472
00:28:57,640 --> 00:28:58,799
you need to give me your phone number.

473
00:28:58,799 --> 00:28:59,640
In a few days,

474
00:28:59,799 --> 00:29:00,240
we might need you

475
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:01,519
to come to the station as a witness.

476
00:29:02,519 --> 00:29:03,920
Sure, absolutely.

477
00:29:10,359 --> 00:29:11,319
This should be the place.

478
00:29:12,240 --> 00:29:12,880
Make the call.

479
00:29:18,039 --> 00:29:18,920
Hello? I'm here.

480
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:19,559
Where are you?

481
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:22,759
Could you bring it inside for me?

482
00:29:23,160 --> 00:29:24,559
Look, I'm just the driver.

483
00:29:24,559 --> 00:29:25,759
I'm not a courier.

484
00:29:27,039 --> 00:29:27,680
How about this, then?

485
00:29:28,039 --> 00:29:29,400
Wait for me by the entrance.

486
00:29:29,839 --> 00:29:30,559
I'll be right out.

487
00:29:31,039 --> 00:29:31,799
All right, sure.

488
00:29:34,559 --> 00:29:35,400
This is the spot.

489
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:36,559
He's coming out right now.

490
00:29:40,119 --> 00:29:40,599
Go deliver it.

491
00:29:44,559 --> 00:29:45,839
All right, I'll go.

492
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,400
This is yours, right?

493
00:30:02,799 --> 00:30:03,400
Thanks.

494
00:30:03,839 --> 00:30:04,519
No problem at all.

495
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:24,119
Hello?

496
00:30:25,599 --> 00:30:26,000
Who's this?

497
00:30:28,079 --> 00:30:28,720
Yeah, got it already.

498
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:31,640
If it's good, I'll get more from you next time.

499
00:30:33,319 --> 00:30:33,720
Bye.

500
00:30:34,480 --> 00:30:34,759
Alright.

501
00:30:59,480 --> 00:30:59,920
Come on.

502
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:39,680
What are you doing?

503
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:44,160
Police.

504
00:31:44,599 --> 00:31:45,839
There might be drug suspects inside.

505
00:31:46,160 --> 00:31:46,759
Hurry, call the police!

506
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:48,319
Okay.

507
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:33,319
Police! Get down, don't move!

508
00:32:51,039 --> 00:32:51,839
I've got a situation here.

509
00:32:51,839 --> 00:32:52,400
Send backup right now!

510
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:17,839
What are you doing?

511
00:33:17,839 --> 00:33:18,359
What are you doing?

512
00:33:18,559 --> 00:33:19,119
Stop!

513
00:33:30,359 --> 00:33:30,960
Put him in the car.

514
00:33:43,359 --> 00:33:44,319
You're a trained fighter, brother.

515
00:33:44,720 --> 00:33:45,440
If it weren't for you,

516
00:33:45,799 --> 00:33:47,200
I'd be lying in a hospital bed by now.

517
00:33:47,440 --> 00:33:49,319
Protecting public safety is our duty.

518
00:33:50,480 --> 00:33:53,279
Am I considered a courageous citizen?

519
00:33:53,319 --> 00:33:54,960
Is there some kind of reward for that?

520
00:33:56,880 --> 00:33:57,519
Don't worry.

521
00:33:57,880 --> 00:33:59,279
I'll definitely report your heroic deed

522
00:33:59,279 --> 00:34:00,559
to the relevant authorities.

523
00:34:01,599 --> 00:34:01,960
By the way,

524
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:04,039
drug dealers and users nowadays

525
00:34:04,039 --> 00:34:05,440
keep finding new ways to commit crimes.

526
00:34:05,720 --> 00:34:06,559
In your daily routine,

527
00:34:06,559 --> 00:34:07,599
please keep a close watch.

528
00:34:07,599 --> 00:34:08,400
If you notice anything suspicious,

529
00:34:08,559 --> 00:34:09,760
report it to the police right away.

530
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,000
Yes, Officer.

531
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:14,559
We'll be heading out now.

532
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:20,440
Not bad, Officer Li.

533
00:34:20,880 --> 00:34:22,199
Cracking a case while taking a ride-share.

534
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:25,360
They were using Psychedelic Blues.

535
00:34:25,880 --> 00:34:26,719
We'll have our hands full again.

536
00:34:29,480 --> 00:34:29,920
Hold on a second.

537
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:35,199
Uncle?

538
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:36,639
It's your aunt.

539
00:34:37,239 --> 00:34:38,559
When are you and Tian Xin getting here?

540
00:34:38,960 --> 00:34:39,960
The food's getting cold.

541
00:34:41,239 --> 00:34:42,159
Tian Xin isn't there yet?

542
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:44,639
Didn't you say she was coming with you?

543
00:34:45,039 --> 00:34:46,559
She told me she was heading over first.

544
00:34:48,039 --> 00:34:49,079
Hold on, give me a moment.

545
00:34:49,079 --> 00:34:50,119
I'll give her a call.

546
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:54,440
He's worked himself into a daze.

547
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:56,400
That boy...

548
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:21,119
Where are you?

549
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:25,960
Tian Xin.

550
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:29,840
Hey, Li Xiao.

551
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:31,719
Something came up, so I can't make it today.

552
00:35:32,639 --> 00:35:33,760
What's wrong? Are you okay?

553
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:37,960
Did something come up in your checkup?

554
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:38,800
No.

555
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:42,840
I really have an emergency. I can't make it.

556
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:44,320
Let's do it another day.

557
00:36:10,159 --> 00:36:10,639
Auntie,

558
00:36:11,880 --> 00:36:13,119
Tian Xin and I

559
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:15,840
won't be able to make it over today.

560
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:18,039
I'm really sorry.

561
00:36:18,159 --> 00:36:20,239
Auntie, could you please let Uncle know?

562
00:36:21,719 --> 00:36:22,079
What's wrong?

563
00:36:26,079 --> 00:36:27,920
Xiao, if you have something to deal with at home,

564
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:28,880
go ahead.

565
00:36:29,119 --> 00:36:29,840
I've got things covered here.

566
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:32,920
We must track down the drug dealers ASAP.

567
00:36:33,119 --> 00:36:33,800
Let's hurry.

568
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:36,920
This kid...

569
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:38,599
Why did he cancel on us all of a sudden?

570
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:43,519
What's the matter?

571
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:45,079
Did the young couple have a fight?

572
00:36:46,679 --> 00:36:47,719
How should I know?

573
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:49,599
Forget it, let's just eat.

574
00:36:51,079 --> 00:36:51,679
Great.

575
00:36:52,039 --> 00:36:53,800
This whole table of food will go to waste again.

576
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:57,000
What else can we do?

577
00:36:57,119 --> 00:36:58,880
Young people are busy these days.

578
00:36:59,079 --> 00:37:00,920
We can't force them to come over.

579
00:37:06,079 --> 00:37:06,760
My chest...

580
00:37:11,039 --> 00:37:12,440
Why is it that whenever Li Xiao calls,

581
00:37:13,119 --> 00:37:14,039
it feels tight?

582
00:37:14,239 --> 00:37:16,519
You're just overthinking it.

583
00:37:19,159 --> 00:37:20,320
Why do I suddenly feel like

584
00:37:21,519 --> 00:37:22,800
something's not right?

585
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:25,760
Why don't you call Li Xiao again

586
00:37:26,039 --> 00:37:27,159
and ask what's going on?

587
00:37:27,239 --> 00:37:29,039
Nothing's wrong. You're just...

588
00:37:32,199 --> 00:37:33,800
Wait here. I'll get your medicine.

589
00:37:39,559 --> 00:37:40,559
When we were tailing Liang Wenbiao,

590
00:37:41,440 --> 00:37:42,679
this Toyota van

591
00:37:42,920 --> 00:37:44,719
was trailing right behind Team A the whole time.

592
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:47,079
If I'm not mistaken,

593
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:49,400
the one who told Liang Wenbiao to abort

594
00:37:50,079 --> 00:37:51,400
was probably someone in this van.

595
00:37:53,039 --> 00:37:54,679
Could it really be Four-Legged Snake's men?

596
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:57,000
Captain Lu,

597
00:37:58,599 --> 00:37:59,559
the drug users from the villa

598
00:37:59,679 --> 00:38:00,400
have all been brought back.

599
00:38:01,519 --> 00:38:02,440
What about the ride-share driver?

600
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:03,880
For now, there's no indication

601
00:38:03,880 --> 00:38:05,440
that he knowingly transported drugs.

602
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:07,719
Once we interrogate them, we'll know for sure.

603
00:38:08,039 --> 00:38:09,760
I've contacted the ride-share platform.

604
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:11,559
They're coming to assist our investigation.

605
00:38:11,760 --> 00:38:12,679
They should be here soon.

606
00:38:13,599 --> 00:38:14,880
You two, look into

607
00:38:14,880 --> 00:38:16,199
the drug supplier immediately.

608
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:18,039
If anything looks off, make the arrest.

609
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:19,000
Understood.

610
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:55,119
What... What do you want?

611
00:39:11,079 --> 00:39:12,320
Did your cop boyfriend

612
00:39:12,880 --> 00:39:15,360
bug Xu Duoduo's place?

613
00:39:25,360 --> 00:39:26,199
I don't know!

614
00:39:26,639 --> 00:39:27,559
I don't know anything!

615
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:31,880
I lost a brother,

616
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:35,159
and I don't know if my boss is alive or dead.

617
00:39:35,800 --> 00:39:37,320
All of this is because of you.

618
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:40,480
So you have to die.

619
00:39:43,039 --> 00:39:43,880
I don't know!

620
00:39:44,480 --> 00:39:45,719
This has nothing to do with me!

621
00:39:46,559 --> 00:39:47,880
I don't know anything!

622
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:49,960
Please, I beg you!

623
00:39:59,119 --> 00:39:59,559
I'm sorry.

624
00:40:02,039 --> 00:40:03,519
I have to answer to my brother.

625
00:40:40,519 --> 00:40:41,239
Keep her alive for now.

626
00:40:57,639 --> 00:40:58,559
We looked into

627
00:40:58,760 --> 00:41:00,400
the ride-hailing number you provided.

628
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:03,000
It's a temporary virtual number.

629
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:05,199
The owner must have thought

630
00:41:05,280 --> 00:41:06,840
this would hide his real identity.

631
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:08,519
But on our back end,

632
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:10,360
it's very easy to trace

633
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:12,159
the number linked to the virtual account.

634
00:41:12,519 --> 00:41:14,599
Plus, when using ride-hailing services,

635
00:41:14,719 --> 00:41:16,559
real-name verification is mandatory.

636
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:19,480
This is the person you're looking for.

637
00:41:20,039 --> 00:41:21,559
His phone and ID numbers are right here.

638
00:41:23,840 --> 00:41:24,480
He Bo.

639
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:26,880
Have the info center look into him now.

640
00:41:27,679 --> 00:41:28,079
On it.

641
00:41:29,559 --> 00:41:30,440
We also checked

642
00:41:30,440 --> 00:41:31,440
the user named Xiao Ran.

643
00:41:32,199 --> 00:41:33,440
He frequently creates secondary accounts.

644
00:41:34,159 --> 00:41:35,159
Through these accounts,

645
00:41:35,199 --> 00:41:37,079
he hails rides extremely often.

646
00:41:37,679 --> 00:41:39,239
Sometimes he'll use different accounts

647
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:41,400
to hail different rides at the same time.

648
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:42,840
Obviously,

649
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:44,840
his purpose isn't actually to take a ride.

650
00:41:46,679 --> 00:41:47,760
Then right now, we also need

651
00:41:47,760 --> 00:41:50,480
all destinations this person went to.

652
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:52,920
No problem.

653
00:41:53,079 --> 00:41:53,880
Once we pull up the records,

654
00:41:53,880 --> 00:41:55,000
we'll fax them to you as soon as possible.

655
00:41:55,920 --> 00:41:57,079
Is it possible for these users

656
00:41:57,079 --> 00:41:58,000
to use someone else's ID

657
00:41:58,000 --> 00:41:59,199
to register an account?

658
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:00,880
If that were the case,

659
00:42:01,039 --> 00:42:01,679
then this person

660
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:03,519
must also use someone else's bank account.

661
00:42:03,639 --> 00:42:04,800
Because ride fares

662
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:06,679
must go through payment apps

663
00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:08,920
to be deducted directly from bank cards.

664
00:42:14,599 --> 00:42:15,159
Understood.

665
00:42:15,599 --> 00:42:17,320
Alright. Thank you both for coming in today

666
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,360
to assist our investigation.

667
00:42:18,719 --> 00:42:20,880
If we need any further information later,

668
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:21,800
I'll reach out to you again.

669
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:23,239
Don't mention it.

670
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:23,920
Thank you.

671
00:42:24,360 --> 00:42:24,800
You're welcome.

672
00:42:39,360 --> 00:42:39,880
What's your take?

673
00:42:42,679 --> 00:42:46,719
With various new messaging apps nowadays,

674
00:42:46,719 --> 00:42:48,760
new ways of dealing drugs keep emerging.

675
00:42:48,920 --> 00:42:50,000
However, the focus of our case this time

676
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:51,159
is that the drugs we seized

677
00:42:51,159 --> 00:42:52,360
are all the new Psychedelic Blues.

678
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:53,920
So I think these drugs

679
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:55,320
must be linked to Four-Legged Snake

680
00:42:55,320 --> 00:42:56,719
and Chen Hai's crew.

681
00:42:59,760 --> 00:43:01,199
Although they're cunning,

682
00:43:01,480 --> 00:43:03,599
they're leaving more and more slip-ups.

683
00:43:04,639 --> 00:43:06,480
What we knew about the case before

684
00:43:06,480 --> 00:43:07,480
was probably just the tip of the iceberg.

685
00:43:07,719 --> 00:43:08,800
But now, that iceberg

686
00:43:10,119 --> 00:43:11,519
is gradually surfacing.

687
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:13,519
Captain Lu.

688
00:43:13,960 --> 00:43:15,079
Through the ID information,

689
00:43:15,079 --> 00:43:16,000
we tracked down this person.

690
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:17,800
He's already dead.

691
00:43:20,239 --> 00:43:20,760
Dead?
